 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Good to help him. Can he use the lift for a few minutes, or is his hip too sore? Then plan a circuit of the ground floor. Start with the front door, then the kitchen, bathroom, and the couch. Yes, in the middle of the landing. That way he can stop if he gets tired. Ask him to take the lift up, and walk downstairs if he can. That's the goal. Take your time with him, and don't plan too much. A short, simple day is easier for everyone.",
